{{#handoff_context.target}}
Keep the current handoff context updated at milestones in {{>handoff-context-target}}.

{{#equals}}JSON{{handoff_context.format}}
The context is a shared JSON object. Keep global top-level sections intact and update only `worktrees.{{worktree.name}}` for this worktree. Root uses `worktrees.root`. A worktree entry may hold its path, issue, phase, plan, task metadata, next steps, milestone, and handoff instructions.
{{/equals}}

{{#equals}}YAML{{handoff_context.format}}
The context is a shared YAML mapping. Keep global top-level sections intact and update only `worktrees.{{worktree.name}}` for this worktree. Root uses `worktrees.root`. A worktree entry may hold its path, issue, phase, plan, task metadata, next steps, milestone, and handoff instructions.
{{/equals}}

{{#equals}}JSON{{handoff_context.format}}
Because this is a client-side shared file, protect every update with the adjacent lock `{{handoff-context-path}}.lock`:

1. Acquire the lock exclusively. If it already exists and its modification time is less than one minute old, wait and retry; if it is at least one minute old, treat it as inactive and replace it.
2. Write only `{{worktree.name}}` to the lock after acquiring it.
3. Reread and validate the current JSON object. Merge only `worktrees.{{worktree.name}}`, retaining every other top-level entry and every other worktree entry.
4. Atomically replace the context file with the merged JSON, then remove only the lock you acquired.
{{/equals}}

{{#equals}}YAML{{handoff_context.format}}
Because this is a client-side shared file, protect every update with the adjacent lock `{{handoff-context-path}}.lock`:

1. Acquire the lock exclusively. If it already exists and its modification time is less than one minute old, wait and retry; if it is at least one minute old, treat it as inactive and replace it.
2. Write only `{{worktree.name}}` to the lock after acquiring it.
3. Reread and validate the current YAML mapping. Merge only `worktrees.{{worktree.name}}`, retaining every other top-level entry and every other worktree entry.
4. Atomically replace the context file with the merged YAML, then remove only the lock you acquired.
{{/equals}}

{{#notequals}}JSON{{handoff_context.format}}
{{#notequals}}YAML{{handoff_context.format}}
This handoff target is not a structured JSON or YAML document, so it cannot carry worktree-specific handoff state.
{{/notequals}}
{{/notequals}}

Do not assume Guide can lock or update this client filesystem path itself.

{{#equals}}JSON{{handoff_context.format}}
Available worktree guidance: {{#resource}}worktree/list{{/resource}},
{{#resource}}worktree/new{{/resource}}, and {{#resource}}worktree/use{{/resource}}.
{{/equals}}
{{#equals}}YAML{{handoff_context.format}}
Available worktree guidance: {{#resource}}worktree/list{{/resource}},
{{#resource}}worktree/new{{/resource}}, and {{#resource}}worktree/use{{/resource}}.
{{/equals}}
{{/handoff_context.target}}
{{^handoff_context.target}}
Handoff context is explicitly disabled for the current project.
{{/handoff_context.target}}
